<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Negus nagast</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as king of kings</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Negus nagast, meaning king of kings, was the title of the Aksumite and later Ethiopian monarchs. In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aksumite-empire">Aksumite Empire</a> it signalled a federal structure in which tributary rulers acknowledged Aksumite suzerainty while keeping local authority. Comparable king-of-kings titles appear elsewhere on the site, such as the Gupta <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maharajadhiraja">Maharajadhiraja</a>, the Sasanian shahanshah and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/benin-empire">Benin</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oba-dynasty">Oba</a>'s style as child of the king of kings.</p></div>
